winit 0.30.1..0.30.13: the macOS backend mixes `CGFloat` and `f64`, which differ on 32-bit targets

mrustc on powerpc-apple-darwin (alacritty 0.17.0):

    winit-0.30.13/src/platform_impl/macos/cursor.rs:58:57 error:0: Type mismatch between f32 and f64

`CGFloat` is `f32` on 32-bit targets (objc2-foundation src/geometry.rs), and winit's public
coordinates are `f64`. The backend converts almost everywhere through the generic
`LogicalPosition::new(point.x, point.y).to_physical(scale)` chains, which infer `CGFloat`; four
places assume `CGFloat == f64` (reviewed statically, mrustc reports one error per crate):

- cursor.rs: `NSPoint::new(.. as f64, .. as f64)` for the hotspot;
- view.rs: `NSEvent::magnification` (`CGFloat`) into `PinchGesture { delta: f64 }`;
- window_delegate.rs: `handle_scale_factor_changed(scale_factor: CGFloat)` is called with the `f64`
  from `scale_factor()` and passes it on to `to_physical`/`to_logical` and the `f64` event field,
  so the parameter is `f64`;
- window_delegate.rs: `increments.to_logical::<f64>(..)` feeds `NSSize::new`.

Identities on 64-bit targets. The four sites are the same from 0.30.1 to 0.30.13 (0.30.0 has no
`handle_scale_factor_changed`). Only cursor.rs:58 was seen on the G5; the rest is pre-review.

